{
  "name": "φ⁴ oscillons",
  "description": "Klein–Gordon with a double-well (φ⁴) potential: the vacua are u = −1 and u = +1. Bubbles of the +1 vacuum collapse, and instead of vanishing they settle into oscillons: lumps that pulse for a very long time, shedding only a little radiation. Domain walls between the vacua are kinks that straighten and shrink. The field is reversible apart from a little viscosity (nu) that damps grid-scale ripples; raise gamma to add friction, or set nu = 0 for pure conservative dynamics. The seed brush (u = 2π) is a big kick; paint gamma to make absorbing regions.",
